  WHY THIS EXISTS
  ================
  DROID_DONOR_PATCH_GATE_1: guy762.mm.kotorcore ("Star Wars KotOR Resources and
  Materials") and guy762.kotorweapons ("Star Wars KotOR Weapons and Armor")
  both ship XML that references ABF's ("ABF: Artificial Beings Framework",
  packageId Killathon.ArtificialBeings) `ArtificialBeings.*` C# classes with NO
  MayRequire guard against ABF itself. If ABF (and its SynCore add-on,
  Killathon.ArtificialBeings.SynCore, which depends on ABF core and cannot
  outlive it) ever retire (WEAPONS_DONOR_RETIREMENT_1 / DROID_SYSTEM_BUILD_1's
  eventual plan), every site below throws "could not find class" at load.

  🔴 CRITICAL GATING CORRECTION, caught during this pass's own validate run:
  ABF is STILL ACTIVE right now and these are, right now, REAL, WORKING
  mechanics (a droid's ABF "Reprogrammable" pawnState, the recharge cells'
  actual need-offset, the Baragwin trader's droid stock). An early draft of
  this file gated each Remove on "the donor mod (kotorcore/kotorweapons) is
  active" — which is true TODAY, meaning it would have fired immediately and
  silently broken live ABF functionality the moment this patch deployed, long
  before ABF ever retires. That is backwards. The correct gate is the
  INVERSE: fire the Remove only once ABF is GONE (PatchOperationFindMod's
  <nomatch> branch, confirmed real via Verse/PatchOperationFindMod.cs — match
  fires when found, nomatch fires when absent). Every operation below is
  dormant today (ABF is active -> nomatch never fires) and activates itself
  automatically the moment ABF leaves ModsConfig.xml, which is exactly what
  "safe to retire ABF" requires and nothing more.

  SCOPE OF THIS FILE — sites 2-10 of the 11 catalogued in
  infrastructure/state/items/DROID_DONOR_PATCH_GATE_1.md. All nine are inert-
  once-ABF-is-gone metadata/mechanic-offset list entries the item file itself
  calls "clean, isolated cuts" needing no design replacement. Deliberately
  NOT included: Site 1 (guy762_KotORDroidBase's CompCoherenceNeed + its
  ParentName="ABF_Thing_Synstruct_HumanlikeBase" inheritance) — that one is a
  live mechanic plus an inheritance-chain dependency that needs the
  Droidworks Need_Power replacement (design/Jawa/droid_system_build_spec.md
  §3 unit 1) ported onto guy762.KotORDroids first; that port hasn't happened
  yet (DROID_SYSTEM_BUILD_1's own "port manifest... waves 1-3" criterion is
  still open). Patching Site 1 now would silently strip a real need with no
  replacement even after ABF retires — a design call reserved for that item.

  RE-VERIFIED AGAINST LIVE WORKSHOP COPIES 2026-09-01 (not just the item
  doc's citations — mod updates shift lines):
    - Sites 3-4: the item doc cited PawnKindDef Name="guy762_RogueDroidPawnKindBase"
      for site 3. The LIVE file (guy762.mm.kotorcore workshop 3254370945,
      1.6/AdditionalMods/_DroidsBase/Defs/PawnKinds_RogueDroidsBase.xml) has
      no such Name anywhere — the two abstract PawnKindDefs are actually
      Name="KotORDroidBase_good" (site 3) and Name="SWCPDroidBase_bad"
      (site 4, matches the doc). Xpaths below use the verified live names.
    - Sites 2, 5, 6, 7-10: line numbers and content otherwise match the item
      doc's citations exactly.
    - NEW FINDING beyond the original 11-site catalog: Site 2's xpath
      (Name="guy762_DroidPawnKindBase") also matches a SECOND, independent
      copy of the same modExtensions/li inside guy762.KotORDroids' own
      PawnKinds_PlayerDroids.xml (workshop 3047371944) — RimWorld merges
      same-Name/defName nodes from every active mod into one document before
      a patch's xpath runs, so this one operation correctly reaches both
      copies without a second xpath. Confirmed via validate_patch.py's own
      "2 match(es) across 2 mod folders" report.
    - NEW FINDING, also beyond the catalog: sites 7-10 (kotorweapons' trader
      stock) are NOT actually "currently moot" as the item doc states.
      guy762.kotorweapons itself is inactive, but mandrake.rsw.armoury
      already carries its own absorbed, ACTIVE copy of the same
      guy762_TraderKind_baragwin/guy762_BaseTraderKind_baragwin TraderKindDefs
      with the identical unguarded ArtificialBeings.StockGenerator_Colonists
      entries (src/RimStarWars/Armoury/Defs/Absorbed_KotorWeapons/TraderKindDefs/).
      Gating on "Star Wars KotOR Weapons and Armor" being active would never
      fire against this absorbed copy at all. Fixed by gating on ABF's
      absence instead (see the correction above) — that condition is correct
      regardless of which of the two copies (donor or absorbed) happens to be
      loaded, or even if both are.

  NOT YET DONE, on purpose:
    - validate_patch.py against a dump captured with ABF actually removed
      (item's own verify step 3) — that needs a mod-list change and a
      restart, out of scope for this offline pass. Validated here only
      against the CURRENT (ABF-present) dump: confirms every match xpath is
      real and well-formed, but cannot exercise the <nomatch> branch itself
      (ABF is active in this dump, so every operation's <match> branch is
      what actually ran during validation — the info log below reflects
      that, not the dormant <nomatch> content).
    - Cold-load verification with ABF actually off (item's verify step 4).
  Both remain open in DROID_DONOR_PATCH_GATE_1's own criteria.
  ============================================================================
